ation, forces a specific response from my opponent, and is the book move in this situation.\n\n\n', 'output': "Evaluation: The move (D, 6) is the strongest choice. It creates a stable horizontal group of three pieces on row D (D4, D5, D6). This formation is structurally sound and limits the opponent's immediate counter-play options to the C-column, whereas (F, 4) would open up the entire left side of the board (Column 3) for the opponent. While (F, 6) restricts the opponent's mobility, it results in a disconnected diagonal shape that is harder to defend. (D, 6) is also the standard strategic response to this board pattern, maximizing stability and control.\n\nReason: It builds a solid 3-piece wall, minimizes the opponent's frontier of valid moves compared to the other options, and maintains piece connectivity.\n\nAnswer: (D, 6)"}
